        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T04:31:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this should be allowed; the 2nd registration should just conflict with the 1st one. When the service comes back the registration should be updated. Otherwise this adds complexity with dependencies between registrations",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2329,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2329,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "e0993af51d52f1096c379f434f2cf0df2bb017c6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d909763_b437be4b",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NsdManagerTest.kt",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 2329,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T06:53:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that this adds additional complexity and we should enforce registering the key and service in the same registration.\n\nBut what about the scenario that a host has multiple services?\n1. Register a host with key.\n2. Register a service using the host with key.  (Should this be considered conflicting for the hostname?) The problem is that when `setPublicKey` we cannot specify if it\u0027s ONLY for the hostname or the service name.\n3. Repeat step 2. (More conflicts?)\n\nOr we should modify the API to specify if the key is for the host or the service. This seems to solve the conflicts.\n\nE.g. \n```java\ninfo.setPublicKey(rData, PUBLIC_KEY_FOR_HOST | PUBLIC_KEY_FOR_SERVICE);\n```\n\n1. Register a host with key.\n2. Register a service using the host with a key for the service.\n3. Repeat step 2.",
      "parentUuid": "b99c340d_a856c58b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2329,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2329,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "e0993af51d52f1096c379f434f2cf0df2bb017c6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74599bbb_8fdcecfb",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NsdManagerTest.kt",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 2329,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T07:08:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also wonder what should be considered as conflict when it comes to hosts.\n\nAccording to the comment above, I guess we won\u0027t allow there to be a registration for the host\u0027s key while there are already other address registrations for the same host. However, currently we\u0027re allowing multiple registrations for the same hostname when key is not involved.\n\nIn the future, what about we only allow a single host registration for the same hostname? That seems to be able to simplify managing the host registrations.",
      "parentUuid": "8d909763_b437be4b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2329,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2329,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "e0993af51d52f1096c379f434f2cf0df2bb017c6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d68e83e2_909bb385",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NsdManagerTest.kt",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 2329,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-02T11:54:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got the consensus via offline discussion that we won\u0027t allow registering the key and the service separately in two registrations.",
      "parentUuid": "74599bbb_8fdcecfb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2329,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2329,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "e0993af51d52f1096c379f434f2cf0df2bb017c6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84f84a4a_639ea817",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NsdManagerTest.kt",
